##############################################################################
#  URFD interlink file
#
#  One line per entry. Each entry specifies a remote reflector to peer with.
#  DNS hostnames and IP addresses are both supported.
#  Remote reflector must also list this reflector in its interlink file.
#  Only listed reflectors may peer: with no entries, no reflector can.
#
#  Format: <Callsign> <Address> <Modules> [Port] [Protocol]
#
#  URF Peering (port 10017):
#    URF270 urf270.example.com EF
#    URF290 ABC                       # DHT only (no address needed)
#
#  XLX Peering (port 10002, requires [XLXPeer] Enable = true):
#    XLX269 xlx269.example.com A
#
#  DCS Peering (two modes, optional protocol field — DCS entries only):
#    DCS002 dcs002.xreflector.net S             # native DCS (port 30051)
#    DCS002 dcs002.xreflector.net S 31000       # native DCS on custom port
#    DCS002 dcs002.xreflector.net S XLX         # XLX protocol (port 10002)
#    DCS002 dcs002.xreflector.net S 10002 XLX   # XLX on explicit port
#
#    Default for DCS entries is native DCS protocol on port 30051.
#    Add "XLX" to use XLX peering instead (requires [XLXPeer] Enable = true).
#    The protocol field is only supported for DCS entries.
#
#  M17 Peering with mrefd reflectors (port 17000, requires [M17] Callsign):
#    M17-QQQ m17-qqq.example.com AB             # mrefd >= 1.0
#    M17-QQQ m17-qqq.example.com AB 17001       # on a custom port
#    M17-QQQL m17-qqq.example.com AB            # legacy mrefd < 1.0 (trailing L)
#    M17-QQQ AB                                 # address from the Ham-DHT
#
#    Without an address the mrefd's DHT document gives address, port and
#    legacy state, and the [M17] Callsign of this reflector is published
#    there for the mrefd in turn. The modules must be the same on both sides,
#    and the mrefd must list this reflector's [M17] Callsign with the same
#    modules in its mrefd.interlink.
#
#############################################################################
